**Definition 4.2 (counted endpoint decoder).** Its supplied data are the
basic memory families0–4 and6, or those coordinates selected from a raw
record $W$, and PublicCode. PublicCode is the fixed original/prior/client/
boot code, $L$, this actually acquired $\Delta(G_{\mathrm{gc}})$ and its
matching installation serialization/layout conventions. It excludes seed
contents, variable inputs, callable family5 payloads, package $I_k$, the
completed list and any acquired Image.

Recover the original private packet from the actual acquired seed using
ARC Definition 6.1's slot-counted syntax conversion and padding to
$2H_0-1$ tokens. Count actual meter receipt cells, excluding L/R, to get
$n$. Start the same encoded irreducible entrance. For $n$ iterations,
interpret its next literal native row as follows.

At a canonical original preparation/boot/capture site, supply its next
bit from that reconstructed packet or the corresponding fixed canonical
public/code word, only at that site. At a variable IN of Lemma 4.1,
the represented prestate already determines $j$, the wire identity $d$
and its table value $w$. If $w\le n$, read the retained symbol at $d$
from the endpoint's13/70 basic cell records. If $n<w$, read the endpoint's
unique matching pending site/bit. Reject a missing, nonbinary or
inconsistent field. Execute one Step with that bit, optionally emit the
canonical patch record and tail the countdown. At a non-IN execute its
actual Step without a supplied bit. Never execute a row after $n$.

All accesses are finite list lookup by reconstructed identities. No live
source, live meter-end scan or current token is used. Emit the consumed
typed reservoir prefix, literal history, raw endpoint and optional
patch list. Selection of family5 is performed only afterwards by
Definition 3.2. An M-body decoder then reselects and compares all seven
families, rather than treating its parsed relation annotations as input.

